"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a lead from Sarah Tan in the Analytics Department. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th. Initially, the budget for phase one was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and the integration of real-time analytics. An additional $55,000 was allocated for a compliance plan, and $15,000 was approved for training programs for the coding team and project managers. The project involves gathering innovative ideas, particularly from R&D, to leverage AI in enhancing data visualization tools. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase for a prototype focused on secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, have been updated and will be effective from January next year. A celebration for the milestone is planned for October 10th."
